-- Example Pre-/Postcondition Constraints for the Methodologist Template
--
-- Unlike constraints.ocl (which uses OCL# invariants, "inv"), this file demonstrates the
-- pre-/postcondition syntax ("pre" / "post") of the same OCL# language, applied to the
-- metaclasses already mapped to Reactions in ProjectReactionConstraints.buildRegistry()
-- (see tools.vitruv.methodologisttemplate.consistency.registry). It exists to exercise the
-- Reaction-Constraint Registry workflow end-to-end with pre/post constraints specifically,
-- as requested for manual testing.
--
-- KNOWN LIMITATION (tracked upstream, not in this project): as of the vitruvocl-language
-- 0.1.0-SNAPSHOT build currently used here, the evaluator's EvaluationVisitor implements
-- visitInvCS(...) but has no visitPreCS(...) / visitPostCS(...) override. "pre" and "post"
-- blocks therefore parse and type-check correctly (a genuine type error still fails, see
-- getFailedConstraints()) but are never evaluated for truthiness -- every pre/post constraint
-- below is currently reported as SATISFIED regardless of its body, even the deliberately
-- self-contradictory ones. This is expected to be fixed upstream; once visitPreCS/visitPostCS
-- are implemented, the constraints below should start reporting real violations without any
-- change needed on this side -- ConstraintRef/ReactionConstraintRegistry/
-- ConstraintEvaluationCoordinator/VitruvOCLGatewayImpl only match on (contextType,
-- constraintName), the same way for "inv", "pre", and "post".
--
-- Syntax notes (OCL#):
--   - context <Namespace>::<Metaclass> pre <ConstraintName>:  -- intended: before a Reaction fires
--   - context <Namespace>::<Metaclass> post <ConstraintName>: -- intended: after a Reaction fires
--   - @severity / @message work exactly as with "inv" (see constraints.ocl for the full syntax
--     notes; they are not repeated here).

-- Precondition for ComponentInsertedIntoSystemReaction / ComponentRenamedReaction:
-- a Component must have a non-empty name before it is synced into model2.
context model::Component pre ComponentHasNameBeforeSync:
    @severity CRITICAL
    @message "Component must have a non-empty name before it is synced to model2"
    self.name <> ""

-- Postcondition for ComponentInsertedIntoSystemReaction:
-- after the reaction fires, every Component must have exactly one corresponding Entity.
context model::Component post ComponentHasCorrespondingEntityAfterSync:
    @severity CRITICAL
    @message "Component {self.name} must have exactly one corresponding Entity in model2 after sync"
    model2::Entity.allInstances().select(~).size() == 1

-- Postcondition for ComponentRenamedReaction:
-- after the reaction fires, the corresponding Entity's name must match the Component's new name.
context model2::Entity post EntityNameMatchesComponentAfterRename:
    @severity MAJOR
    @message "Entity {self.name} must match the name of its corresponding Component after a rename"
    model::Component.allInstances().select(~).forAll(c | c.name == self.name)

-- Precondition for LinkInsertedIntoSystemReaction / ComponentInsertedIntoLinkReaction:
-- a Link must reference at least one Component before it is considered ready to sync.
context model::Link pre LinkHasAtLeastOneComponentBeforeSync:
    @severity MAJOR
    @message "{self} must reference at least one Component before it is synced to model2"
    self.components.size() >= 1

-- Postcondition for LinkInsertedIntoSystemReaction / ComponentInsertedIntoLinkReaction:
-- after the reactions fire, the corresponding Link in model2 must reference at least two entities.
context model2::Link post LinkHasAtLeastTwoEntitiesAfterSync:
    @severity MAJOR
    @message "{self} must reference at least two entities after sync"
    self.entities.size() >= 2
